[{:db/id 17592186142780 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02df687b-3c38-56ea-bcbb-7b6992abb8b8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-02df687b-3c38-56ea-bcbb-7b6992abb8b8" :question/id #uuid "02df687b-3c38-56ea-bcbb-7b6992abb8b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134231" :question/problem "Matt and Andrea each bought $6$ ounces of salted peanuts and $4$ ounces of unsalted peanuts. In total, they bought$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ounces of peanuts." :question/worked-solution "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total amount of peanuts.\n\nSince each of them bought $6$ ounces of salted peanuts and $4$ ounces of unsalted peanuts, the amount of peanuts they purchased, in ounces, is:\n\n$$\n{{6}_{⏟}}_{\\text{salted peanuts}}+{{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{unsalted peanuts}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person purchased this amount of peanuts, and there are $2$ people, we must multiply the amount of peanuts by $2.$ Therefore, the total amount of peanuts is:\n\n$$\n{{(6+4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6+4)\\times 2 & =(6+4)\\times 2 \\\\  & =10\\times 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n10\\times 2=20\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5349a1c7-9dd6-5f93-9b66-8b75dd18d825"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5349a1c7-9dd6-5f93-9b66-8b75dd18d825" :answer-field/id #uuid "5349a1c7-9dd6-5f93-9b66-8b75dd18d825" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29" :answer-field/choices ["answer-48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29" :answer/id #uuid "48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059859 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b88dbf04-dd80-54e8-8fde-e4783f40c410"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b88dbf04-dd80-54e8-8fde-e4783f40c410" :question/id #uuid "b88dbf04-dd80-54e8-8fde-e4783f40c410" :question/math-academy-id "q-134232" :question/problem "Carla has $12$ packages of almonds, each weighing $42$ ounces. In total, Carla has$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ounces of almonds." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total amount of almonds, we need to multiply $12$ by $42.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 2=24\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 40=480\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}24+480=504\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12\\times 42=504.$\n\nTherefore, Carla has $504$ ounces of almonds in total." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d9ab1077-8f29-5a4e-a28a-f16902739e34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9ab1077-8f29-5a4e-a28a-f16902739e34" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ab1077-8f29-5a4e-a28a-f16902739e34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e" :answer/id #uuid "b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "504" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073698 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c1e68ffc-d3ca-5167-817a-cc856c132a73"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c1e68ffc-d3ca-5167-817a-cc856c132a73" :question/id #uuid "c1e68ffc-d3ca-5167-817a-cc856c132a73" :question/math-academy-id "q-134234" :question/problem "Robert bought $3$ pounds of walnuts while Susan bought $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts. How many walnuts did they buy together in total? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nThey bought$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of walnuts in total." :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of walnuts Robert and Susan bought together in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n3+\\frac{17}{9}\n$$\n\nTo add $3$ and $\\frac{17}{9},$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $9.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $9$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 9}{1\\times 9}=\\frac{27}{9}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{9}+\\frac{17}{9}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{9}+\\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{27+17}{9}=\\frac{44}{9}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n44÷9=4\\,\\text{R}\\,8=4\\,\\frac{8}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, they bought $4\\,\\frac{8}{9}$ pounds of walnuts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61d4181d-edef-5c2f-bb3f-ce5a078247b4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61d4181d-edef-5c2f-bb3f-ce5a078247b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "61d4181d-edef-5c2f-bb3f-ce5a078247b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c" :answer/id #uuid "186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\frac{8}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186073826 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-357eb628-a446-5e21-9526-dabfe7335132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-357eb628-a446-5e21-9526-dabfe7335132" :question/id #uuid "357eb628-a446-5e21-9526-dabfe7335132" :question/math-academy-id "q-134235" :question/problem "Of the $3$ pounds of walnuts that Robert bought, he gave $\\frac{3}{5}$ pounds to his granddaughter Sophia. As a mixed number, Robert has{{field-1}}\npounds of walnuts remaining." :question/worked-solution "To find out how many walnuts Robert had remaining, we must calculate the difference $3-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{3}{5}$ from $3,$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{15}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{15-3}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n12÷5=2\\,\\text{R}\\,2=2\\,\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Robert had $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of walnuts remaining." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-34368c67-3db4-5d2a-b4a5-7e644a1384c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34368c67-3db4-5d2a-b4a5-7e644a1384c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "34368c67-3db4-5d2a-b4a5-7e644a1384c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59" :answer/id #uuid "f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198431 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-994437db-5e6c-52cd-85e4-193a53ab9c7f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-994437db-5e6c-52cd-85e4-193a53ab9c7f" :question/id #uuid "994437db-5e6c-52cd-85e4-193a53ab9c7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134236" :question/problem "After Sophia takes her share of walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is{{field-1}}\nthan Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{17}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Robert has $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of walnuts remaining, and Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ pounds of walnuts.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 9=45.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}=\\frac{12\\times 9}{5\\times 9}=\\frac{108}{45}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{17}{9}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{17\\times 5}{9\\times 5}=\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{108}{45}$ and $\\frac{85}{45}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $108>85,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{108}{45}>\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Sophia takes her walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is $>$ than Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}>\\frac{17}{9}.$\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8fcd58ca-53e4-51a1-8c9a-e0b485e4a754" "answer-field-89dc9221-5a2e-543b-a0cb-442c6540822e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8fcd58ca-53e4-51a1-8c9a-e0b485e4a754" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcd58ca-53e4-51a1-8c9a-e0b485e4a754" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c" :answer/id #uuid "4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89dc9221-5a2e-543b-a0cb-442c6540822e" :answer-field/id #uuid "89dc9221-5a2e-543b-a0cb-442c6540822e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d" :answer/id #uuid "f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142796 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-56c0d0ac-e441-53cb-9b72-c25279d28ac0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-56c0d0ac-e441-53cb-9b72-c25279d28ac0" :question/id #uuid "56c0d0ac-e441-53cb-9b72-c25279d28ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-134237" :question/problem "Susan ate $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the walnuts that she bought. What **exact** amount of walnuts did she eat?\n\n*Remember that Susan bought $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts.*\n\nSusan ate$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of walnuts." :question/worked-solution "We know that Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts.\n\nTo calculate the amount that she ate, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{3}$ by $\\frac{17}{9}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{1\\times 17}{3\\times 9}=\\frac{17}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Susan ate $\\frac{17}{27}$ of  a pound of walnuts." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7069eb3-7077-523c-883d-c4e8428dace8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7069eb3-7077-523c-883d-c4e8428dace8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7069eb3-7077-523c-883d-c4e8428dace8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1" :answer/id #uuid "7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
